<h2>INTRODUCTION</h2>
<p>The original Shark Jack devices are powerful, portable network pentesting devices for rapid deployment of payloads. Easy payload updates, situation-aware adaptability and interactivity were skipped in order to optimise for simplicity and speed.</p>
<p><strong>The Shark Jack Display changes everything:</strong> still ultra-portable, still speed-optimised - but with the inclusion of an <strong>OLED display and rocker-switch</strong> - ethernet audits are now interactive.</p>
<p><strong>Interact with payloads in real-time</strong> and see <strong>live results on-screen</strong>. Scan a network, read the output, dig deeper - <b>all on-device, no computer necessary</b>.</p>
<p>The Shark Jack Display natively runs <b>Bash and interactive DuckyScript™</b>: payloads can now request your input, branch on results and drive any Linux network tool.</p>
<p>The device ships with preloaded payloads: over a dozen built-in payloads, and can automatically download new updates.</p>
<p>Finally, sys-admins with two Shark Jacks can use SharkLink™ - to finally get a quick solution the age-old problem: easily tell if there's a route between two different ports.</p>
</div>
